<title>BELGIUM: EU committee to discuss wheat quota.</title>
<headline>EU committee to discuss wheat quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee is expected to discuss the introduction of a quota for high quality and durum wheat on Wednesday, an EU offical said.</p>
<p>&quot;A discussion is listed on modifying regulation 529 of '97 to allow the opening of a quota said to be for 100,000 tonnes of quality wheat and quotas for 106,000 tonnes of durum wheat&quot;, the official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The quota arrangement arises from the GATT (General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade) negotiations following enlargement of the EU and is largely procedural since import duties are already at zero, the official said.</p>
</text>
